user_message:
Compare the candidate edge types against the existing edge type registry.

Classify every candidate into exactly one of the following categories:

EXISTING: An existing type adequately covers the candidate's semantic relationship.

NEW: The candidate expresses a distinct semantic relationship not adequately covered by the registry.

UNCERTAIN: The candidate partially overlaps with an existing type and requires further review.

Compare the relationship definitions, applicability conditions, source roles, target roles, and relationship directions.

Apply the supplied granularity rules and positive and negative examples.

Candidate Edge Types:

[
  {
    "name": "INSPECTS_REFERENCE_ARTIFACT_TO_LEARN_SEMANTICS",
    "definition": "An agent reads or examines a reference artifact (source code, example input, configuration) of the target system in order to learn its exact operational semantics before designing a solution, receiving the artifact content as an observation.",
    "source_description": "An agent inspection/read action directed at a reference artifact of the target system.",
    "target_description": "The observation returning the reference artifact's contents that specify the system's behavior."
  },
  {
    "name": "DERIVES_DESIGN_FROM_OBSERVED_BEHAVIOR",
    "definition": "An agent's design or plan is formulated by explicitly exploiting behavioral details (evaluation order, timing conventions, input/output indexing, step limits) obtained from an earlier observation of the target system.",
    "source_description": "An earlier observation that revealed the operational behavior of the target system.",
    "target_description": "A subsequent agent reasoning step or plan that specifies a design depending on those observed behavioral details."
  },
  {
    "name": "VERIFIES_PREREQUISITE_FOR_PLANNED_ACTION",
    "definition": "Before performing an anticipated action, the agent performs an exploratory check to confirm that a precondition required by that action (such as a tool, binary, or file) is actually available.",
    "source_description": "A planned action whose execution depends on an unverified precondition.",
    "target_description": "An exploratory check action that verifies the availability of the required resource."
  },
  {
    "name": "PRODUCES_DELIVERABLE_VIA_AUTHORED_TOOL",
    "definition": "The agent authors an intermediate program or script whose execution generates the deliverable artifact required by the task, rather than producing the artifact directly.",
    "source_description": "An agent action that writes or defines an intermediate tool or generator program.",
    "target_description": "Execution of that authored tool that produces the required output artifact."
  },
  {
    "name": "CONFORMS_GENERATED_OUTPUT_TO_OBSERVED_FORMAT",
    "definition": "The content of an artifact produced by the agent is structured to match a syntax or interface format that was previously observed in a reference artifact or specification.",
    "source_description": "An earlier observation that established the accepted format or interface rules of the artifact.",
    "target_description": "The generated artifact content that conforms to those observed format rules."
  },
  {
    "name": "REPORTS_ARTIFACT_METRIC_AGAINST_CONSTRAINT",
    "definition": "Execution of the artifact-producing action returns an observation reporting a quantitative property of the produced artifact that is directly comparable to a stated task constraint (such as a size or count limit).",
    "source_description": "Execution of the action that generated the artifact.",
    "target_description": "An observation reporting a measurable property of the produced artifact that indicates compliance with a task constraint."
  }
]

